# ================================================================ Lower Blackrock Spire
# Quest ids, givers, levels, prerequisites, objectives, drops: Polestar's Forever data and its
# Dungeons codex (Blackrock Spire, lower and upper together); prerequisites cross-checked with the
# TrinityCore base: no disagreement (Message to Maxwell 5002 after Bijou's Belongings 5001, Maxwell's
# Mission 5081 after 5002; the others need nothing). Rooms, bosses and how-to: Warcraft Tavern's
# Forever Lower Blackrock Spire dungeon and quest guides (warcrafttavern.com/forever/guides/
# lower-blackrock-spire and .../lower-blackrock-spire-quests, read on 12/11/2026), written from
# Classic (closed in the Forever beta): places inside are to check in game.
# Asked once (`when group 4701`, Put Her Down: no prerequisite, level 55); every later step needs
# `when done lbrs-start`. Flow: Morgan's Vigil (Helendis) -> Flame Crest (Kibler, Ragged John) ->
# the Spire: Hordemar City (Warosh, Bijou and her belongings) -> out to Maxwell and back, the bosses
# left alive (Warcraft Tavern's advice) -> Omokk, Tazz'Alaor (Voone), the Skitterweb Tunnels
# (Smolderweb, the eggs), Urok's Tribute Pile, Halycon, Wyrmthalak -> Warosh -> Flame Crest ->
# Morgan's Vigil.
# Left out: Seal of Ascension (Vaelan: the key of Upper Blackrock Spire, a 10-player dungeon, then
# Emberstrife in Dustwallow Marsh), The Final Tablets (Mosh'aru's chain), Snakestone of the Shadow
# Huntress (Kilram, Winterspring), Deliana's dungeon set quests, General Drakkisath's Demise (Upper
# Blackrock Spire).
step Lower Blackrock Spire (dungeon, optional)
  label lbrs-start
  when group 4701
  tip Lower Blackrock Spire: the orc city in the upper part of Blackrock Mountain, above Blackrock Depths. Levels 55 to 60, bosses 58 to 60: a group of 5 at 58 to 60 (possible from about 56, difficult). The quests come from Morgan's Vigil and Flame Crest, one more from a goblin hidden inside; the run has one short trip out to Morgan's Vigil and back. Alone? Skip it.
  note Keep 9 free quest log slots.
  goto 85.0,68.8 map 1428 "Morgan's Vigil" r 40

step Morgan's Vigil: Helendis Riverhorn
  when done lbrs-start
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Put Her Down: Halycon, the great worg of the Spire. Marshal Maxwell's own quest comes later, through Bijou, a goblin hidden in the dungeon.
  accept 4701                         -- Helendis Riverhorn

step Flame Crest: Kibler and Ragged John
  when done lbrs-start
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Ride north to Flame Crest. Kibler stands inside the cave: his two quests give two pets, the Worg Carrier and the Smolderweb Carrier, and he hands over an Empty Worg Pup Cage. Ragged John, in the camp: Mother's Milk, a rare reward.
  accept 4729                         -- Kibler
  accept 4862                         -- Kibler
  accept 4866                         -- Ragged John

step Lower Blackrock Spire: before going in
  when done lbrs-start
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Into Blackrock Mountain on the Burning Steppes side. Two ways to the portal: the door beside the Blackrock Spire meeting stone and the path up (elites on it), or along the great chain and the wall to the balcony where Bodley stands, then a jump down onto it, with no fight. Inside, the stairs up on the left lead to Upper Blackrock Spire: not this time.
  note In the quest log: Put Her Down (Helendis), Kibler's Exotic Pets and En-Ay-Es-Tee-Why (Kibler), Mother's Milk (Ragged John). Given inside: Urok Doomhowl (Warosh) and Bijou's Belongings (Bijou). Not on this route: Seal of Ascension (Vaelan, inside: the key of Upper Blackrock Spire, a 10-player dungeon), The Final Tablets (the Mosh'aru tablets), Snakestone of the Shadow Huntress (Kilram, Winterspring), Deliana's dungeon set quests (Ironforge).
  goto 33.2,24.9 map 1428 "Blackrock Spire" r 25

step Hordemar City: Warosh and Bijou
  when done lbrs-start
  tip Past the entrance door, Hordemar City. Warosh walks around its first part. Bijou waits on a ledge overlooking the city: one of the ramps down to Tazz'Alaor, the trolls' hall with the purple light, climbs to her. Her belongings are in a small chest tucked in a corner at the bottom of Hordemar City (it has several places). Leave Highlord Omokk, War Master Voone and Overlord Wyrmthalak alive for now: Marshal Maxwell's quest, given for Bijou's message, asks for them.
  accept 4867                         -- Warosh
  accept 5001                         -- Bijou
  collect 12345 quest 5001            -- Bijou's Belongings: a small chest at the bottom of Hordemar City
  turnin 5001                         -- Bijou
  accept 5002

step Message to Maxwell: out and back
  when onquest 5002
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Leave the dungeon without resetting it: as long as the group stays together, the same instance waits, bosses alive (to check in game). Ride to Morgan's Vigil and back, a good quarter of an hour; a hearthstone bound at the Vigil shortens the way there.
  turnin 5002                         -- Marshal Maxwell
  accept 5081

step Lower Blackrock Spire: along the way
  when done lbrs-start
  along until lbrs-end
  tip The Bloodaxe Worg Pups play in Hordemar City and in Halycon's lair: target one and use the Empty Worg Pup Cage. The Spire Spider Eggs lie in the Skitterweb Tunnels, Mother Smolderweb's halls: each egg sac gives 1 to 3, and spiderlings may hatch from them.
  collect 12263 quest 4729            -- Caged Worg Pup
  collect 12530 quest 4862            -- Spire Spider Egg

step Highlord Omokk
  when done lbrs-start
  tip Urok Doomhowl needs a Roughshod Pike: they lean against the wall behind the Scarshield orcs, past the bridge out of Hordemar City. Then the Spirestone ogres: Highlord Omokk (elite 59) and his two guards. His head is for the Urok event: one player with the quest carries the pike and the head.
  collect 12533 optional              -- Roughshod Pike
  kill 9196 quest 5081                -- Highlord Omokk
  collect 12534 optional              -- Omokk's Head

step Tazz'Alaor: War Master Voone
  when done lbrs-start
  tip Down into Tazz'Alaor, the trolls' hall: Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin (elite 59, two priests at her side), then down the great ramp and along the hall to War Master Voone (elite 59, no adds, hits very hard).
  kill 9237 quest 5081                -- War Master Voone

step Skitterweb Tunnels: Mother Smolderweb
  when done lbrs-start
  tip The spiders' tunnels: the eggs for Kibler. Mother Smolderweb (elite 59) waits at the top. Whoever has Mother's Milk lets her poison them, and nobody removes that poison; then kill her. The poison must still be there at Ragged John's: if it would wear off before the end of the run (to check in game), that player goes out right after her and comes back.
  kill 10596 optional                 -- Mother Smolderweb

step Urok's Tribute Pile
  when done lbrs-start
  tip Up the ramp past the tunnels, on the corner of the landing, behind two Spirestone orcs: Urok's Tribute Pile, a heap of skulls. The player with the Roughshod Pike and Omokk's Head stands by it and uses the head: waves of ogres come, then Urok Doomhowl (elite 60). Every 30 seconds, the pike used on the pile kills one ogre outright.
  collect 12712 quest 4867            -- Warosh's Mojo: Urok Doomhowl

step Halycon and Gizrul
  when done lbrs-start
  tip Past Quartermaster Zigris, Halycon's lair: the great worg (elite 59) and her pups. Gizrul the Slavener runs in right after her death: no time to rest in between.
  kill 10220 quest 4701               -- Halycon

step Overlord Wyrmthalak
  when done lbrs-start
  tip The last boss, Overlord Wyrmthalak (elite 60), calls two adds at half health. He drops General Drakkisath's Command for each player: right-click it.
  kill 9568 quest 5081                -- Overlord Wyrmthalak
  accept 5089                         -- General Drakkisath's Command: Overlord Wyrmthalak

step Hordemar City: Warosh
  when complete 4867
  tip Back to the entrance: Warosh walks around the first part of Hordemar City.
  turnin 4867                         -- Warosh

step Flame Crest: Ragged John
  when onquest 4866
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Out of the Spire, north-east to Flame Crest. Ragged John: his talk option, while the poison is still on you. Poison gone? Mother's Milk cannot be done this time: skip this step.
  kill 9563 quest 4866                -- Ragged John: let him milk you
  turnin 4866                         -- Ragged John

step Flame Crest: Kibler's worg pup
  when complete 4729
  zone Burning Steppes
  turnin 4729                         -- Kibler

step Flame Crest: Kibler's spider eggs
  when complete 4862
  zone Burning Steppes
  turnin 4862                         -- Kibler

step Morgan's Vigil: Helendis Riverhorn
  when complete 4701
  zone Burning Steppes
  turnin 4701                         -- Helendis Riverhorn

step Morgan's Vigil: Marshal Maxwell
  when complete 5081
  zone Burning Steppes
  turnin 5081                         -- Marshal Maxwell

step Morgan's Vigil: General Drakkisath's Command
  when onquest 5089
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Maxwell's next quest, General Drakkisath's Demise, is for Upper Blackrock Spire (10 players, the Seal of Ascension to open it): not in this guide.
  turnin 5089                         -- Marshal Maxwell

step Lower Blackrock Spire: quests not done
  label lbrs-end
  when done lbrs-start
  tip What is left of Lower Blackrock Spire in the quest log is for another run: keep it for one, or drop it to free the log.
  abandon 4701 optional
  abandon 4729 optional
  abandon 4862 optional
  abandon 4866 optional
  abandon 4867 optional
  abandon 5081 optional

# ================================================================ Dire Maul
# Quest ids, givers, levels, prerequisites, objectives, drops: Polestar's Forever data and its
# Dungeons codex; prerequisites cross-checked with the TrinityCore base: no disagreement (The
# Treasure of the Shen'dralar after The Madness Within; Shards of the Felvine after A Reliquary of
# Purity, handed in to Rabine Saturna in Group 30; Lethtendris's Web needs nothing, its errand from
# Stormwind or Ironforge is dropped by the compiler). Rooms, bosses and how-to: Warcraft Tavern's
# Forever Dire Maul East and West dungeon and quest guides (warcrafttavern.com/forever/guides/
# dire-maul-east, dire-maul-west, dire-maul-east-quests, dire-maul-west-quests, read on 12/11/2026),
# written from Classic (closed in the Forever beta): places inside are to check in game.
# Asked once (`when group 7488`, Lethtendris's Web: level 54); every later step needs `when done
# dm-start`. Flow: Feathermoon (Latronicus, Runethorn) -> Lariss Pavilion (Azj'Tordin) -> the eastern
# wing (Pusillin and the Crescent Key, Lethtendris, Zevrim, Alzzin and the Felvine) -> out by its
# back door to Azj'Tordin -> the western wing (the five pylons, the Shen'dralar Ancient, Immol'thar,
# Tortheldrin, the Athenaeum) -> Feathermoon -> Moonglade (Rabine, Shards of the Felvine, if taken).
# The Treasure of the Shen'dralar has two versions in the data (7462 for the Alliance, 7877 for
# every race), both after The Madness Within: the guide offers both, optional, and the Ancient gives
# the one Forever uses (to check in game).
# Left out: the northern wing (The Gordok Ogre Suit, Free Knot!, Unfinished Gordok Business, A
# Broken Trap, The Gordok Taste Test: the tribute run), Lorekeeper Lydros's libram quests (black
# diamonds, enchanting shards and other materials), the class books that drop in the dungeon (a
# player's own quest, handed to Lydros), the class quests (Arcane Refreshment, Quel'Serrar, the
# warlock's and paladin's mounts), Isalien (dungeon set).
step Dire Maul (dungeon, optional)
  label dm-start
  when group 7488
  tip Dire Maul: the ruined elf city in the middle of Feralas, three wings. The guide does the eastern one (Warpwood Quarter, 55 to 58), whose imp carries the key of the others, then the western one (Capital Gardens, 58 to 60). A group of 5 at 58 to 60; possible from about 56, difficult. The quests come from Feathermoon Stronghold, the Lariss Pavilion and, if taken in Group 30, Moonglade. Alone? Skip it.
  note Keep 8 free quest log slots. The northern wing (the ogres' tribute) is not in the guide.
  goto 30.3,43.3 map 1444 "Feathermoon Stronghold" r 40

step Feathermoon Stronghold
  when done dm-start
  zone Feralas
  tip Latronicus Moonspear stands in the fort; Scholar Runethorn walks the road through it.
  accept 7488                         -- Latronicus Moonspear
  accept 7482                         -- Scholar Runethorn

step Lariss Pavilion: Azj'Tordin
  when done dm-start
  zone Feralas
  tip The Lariss Pavilion stands north-east of Camp Mojache (Horde), east of Dire Maul: from Feathermoon, the flight to Thalanaar and the road west is the quickest way. Azj'Tordin's book is with Pusillin, the imp at the eastern wing's entrance.
  accept 7441                         -- Azj'Tordin

step Dire Maul: before going in
  when done dm-start
  zone Feralas
  tip Dire Maul stands on the plateau in the middle of Feralas. The eastern wing opens on the east wall of the central courtyard, and from Eldreth Row at the city's gates; both lead to the upper level of the Warpwood Quarter.
  note In the quest log: Lethtendris's Web (Latronicus), Elven Legends (Runethorn), Pusillin and the Elder Azj'Tordin. If taken in Group 30: Shards of the Felvine (Rabine Saturna). A class book found in the dungeon starts a quest of its own: it goes to Lorekeeper Lydros, in the Athenaeum (western wing). Not on this route: the northern wing's quests, Lydros's libram quests.
  goto 59.2,45.1 map 1444 "Dire Maul" r 25

step Warpwood Quarter: Pusillin
  when done dm-start
  tip Pusillin the imp waits by the entrance: speak with him, then chase him through the first rooms, speaking with him each time he stops. He ends on a platform up a ramp near the back door, where he fights (elite 57). He drops Azj'Tordin's Book of Incantations and the Crescent Key, which opens the western and northern wings: one key in the group is enough.
  collect 18261 quest 7441            -- Book of Incantations: Pusillin
  collect 18249 optional              -- Crescent Key: Pusillin

step Warpwood Quarter: Lethtendris
  when done dm-start
  tip Lethtendris (elite 57), a blood elf warlock, fights with her imp Pimgib: interrupt her spells. Her web is for Latronicus.
  collect 18426 quest 7488            -- Lethtendris's Web: Lethtendris

step Warpwood Quarter: Alzzin the Wildshaper
  when done dm-start
  tip Hydrospawn patrols the pool on the next level down. Zevrim Thornhoof (elite 57) sacrifices players on his altar; after him, speak with Old Ironbark: he opens the Conservatory Door. Clear the Warpwood Crushers on the ramp, then Alzzin the Wildshaper (elite 58), who changes shape. Shards of the Felvine: once he is dead, the Felvine behind him drops its shards; loot one, then use the Reliquary of Purity.
  kill 11492 optional                 -- Alzzin the Wildshaper
  collect 18540 quest 5526            -- Sealed Reliquary of Purity: a Felvine Shard in the Reliquary of Purity

step Lariss Pavilion: Azj'Tordin
  when complete 7441
  zone Feralas
  tip The door at the back of Alzzin's room opens with the Crescent Key straight onto the Lariss Pavilion.
  turnin 7441                         -- Azj'Tordin

step Dire Maul West: before going in
  when done dm-start
  zone Feralas
  tip Back to the central courtyard of Dire Maul: the western wing opens on its west wall, with the Crescent Key. Five pylons, great crystals, shield Immol'thar's prison: kill every Arcane Aberration and Mana Remnant around a pylon to shut it down.
  goto 59.2,45.1 map 1444 "Dire Maul" r 25

step Capital Gardens and the Court of the Highborne
  when done dm-start
  tip The first pylon stands in the Capital Gardens, right in front of the entrance. Kill the wandering Ancients before Tendris Warpwood (elite 60), who calls them all. Upstairs, the Court of the Highborne: two more pylons, Illyanna Ravenoak and Magister Kalendris. The Shen'dralar Ancient stands on the bridge of the upper level.
  accept 7461                         -- Shen'dralar Ancient

step Immol'thar and Prince Tortheldrin
  when done dm-start
  tip The last two pylons stand either side of the door of the Prison of Immol'thar: with all five down, its force field is gone. Immol'thar (elite 61) calls adds and moves players to the middle of the room; he enrages at half health. A small tunnel then leads to the Athenaeum: Prince Tortheldrin (elite 60).
  kill 11496 quest 7461               -- Immol'thar
  kill 11486 quest 7461               -- Prince Tortheldrin

step The Athenaeum: Elven Legends
  when done dm-start
  tip The skeletal remains lie on the floor beside Lorekeeper Lydros, in the Athenaeum: choose to mourn the great loss.
  interact 179544 quest 7482          -- Skeletal remains, beside Lorekeeper Lydros

step The Shen'dralar Ancient and his treasure
  when done dm-start
  tip Back to the Shen'dralar Ancient on the bridge of the Court of the Highborne. His next quest sends you to the Treasure of the Shen'dralar, a chest under the ramp of the Athenaeum: take the one he offers.
  turnin 7461                         -- Shen'dralar Ancient
  accept 7462 optional                -- Shen'dralar Ancient
  accept 7877 optional                -- Shen'dralar Ancient: the same quest, the other version
  turnin 7462 optional                -- Treasure of the Shen'dralar, under the ramp of the Athenaeum
  turnin 7877 optional

step Feathermoon Stronghold: Latronicus Moonspear
  when complete 7488
  zone Feralas
  tip Out of Dire Maul, back to Feathermoon Stronghold (the flight from Thalanaar, or the road west and the boat).
  turnin 7488                         -- Latronicus Moonspear

step Feathermoon Stronghold: Scholar Runethorn
  when complete 7482
  zone Feralas
  turnin 7482                         -- Scholar Runethorn

step Moonglade: Rabine Saturna
  when complete 5526
  zone Moonglade
  tip Shards of the Felvine: Rabine Saturna, in her house in Nighthaven. From Feathermoon, the flight to Moonglade.
  turnin 5526                         -- Rabine Saturna

step Dire Maul: quests not done
  label dm-end
  when done dm-start
  tip What is left of Dire Maul in the quest log is for another run: keep it for one, or drop it to free the log.
  abandon 7488 optional
  abandon 7482 optional
  abandon 7441 optional
  abandon 7461 optional

# Groupe Alliance 0.12.0: Shards of the Felvine (5526), taken in Group 30 with its own question,
# when Dire Maul was skipped or the shard not sealed: nothing brings the guide back to Moonglade.
step Shards of the Felvine: not done
  when onquest 5526
  when !complete 5526
  tip Shards of the Felvine is not done and the guide does not go back to Dire Maul: abandon it, or keep it for a run of your own.
  abandon 5526

# ================================================================ Stratholme
# Quest ids, givers, levels, prerequisites, objectives, drops: Polestar's Forever data and its
# Dungeons codex; prerequisites cross-checked with the TrinityCore base: no disagreement (The Active
# Agent after The Flesh Does Not Lie; The Truth Comes Crashing Down, started by the Head of Balnazzar,
# after The Archivist; Above and Beyond after it, then Lord Maxwell Tyrosus and The Argent Hold;
# The Restless Souls 5282 after 5281, handed to Egan in Group 28; Of Love and Family 5848 after 5846,
# handed to Renfray in Group 30). Polestar's data and
# Warcraft Tavern name the tobacco merchant Ezra Grimm (The Great Ezra Grimm); TrinityCore keeps
# the old title, The Great Fras Siabi. Rooms, bosses and how-to: Warcraft Tavern's Forever
# Stratholme (living and undead) dungeon and quest guides (warcrafttavern.com/forever/
# guides/stratholme-living, stratholme-undead, stratholme-living-quests, stratholme-undead-quests,
# read on 12/11/2026), written from Classic (closed in the Forever beta): places inside are to
# check in game.
# Asked at Light's Hope Chapel (`when group 5212`, The Flesh Does Not Lie: level 55); every later
# step needs `when done strat-start`.
# Stratholme, three visits in one instance, as its quest chains ask (Warcraft Tavern: The Archivist
# must be handed in before Balnazzar dies, The Truth Comes Crashing Down before the Baron does):
#   1. the living side, by the main gate: Ezra Grimm, the Scarlet Bastion (Malor's strongbox,
#      Archivist Galford and the painting), Elders' Square (Barthilas: the Key to the City);
#   2. Balnazzar, then a ride to Light's Hope and back;
#   3. the dead side, by the Service Entrance: Aurius, the three ziggurats, Ramstein, the Baron.
# Left out: Menethil's Gift and the rest of Ras Frostwhisper's chain (The Human, Ras Frostwhisper:
# Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands, Light's Hope, Stratholme before the Baron, Scholomance again;
# the TrinityCore base also asks Friendly standing with Caer Darrow, faction 574, for its first
# quest, which Polestar's data does not); Sweet Serenity and Corruption (Winterspring,
# the Crimson Hammersmith and the Black Guard Swordsmith); Dead Man's Plea, Deliana's and Anthion
# Harmon's dungeon set quests; Scholomance (next).
step Stratholme (dungeon, optional)
  label strat-start
  when group 5212
  tip Stratholme: the dead city in the north-west of the Eastern Plaguelands, levels 58 to 60, bosses 57 to 62: a group of 5 at 58 to 60; possible from about 56, difficult. The quests come from Light's Hope Chapel, from Egan in Terrordale and, if taken in Group 30, from Artist Renfray. Its quest chains ask for three visits to the same instance: the living side, then Balnazzar, then the dead side, with rides back to Light's Hope in between. Alone? Skip it.
  note Keep 8 free quest log slots.
  goto 71.7,49.9 map 1423 live "Light's Hope Chapel" r 40

step Light's Hope Chapel: Stratholme
  when done strat-start
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Leonid Barthalomew the Revered stands inside the chapel; Betina Bigglezink, Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff and Smokey LaRue stand around it.
  accept 5212                         -- Betina Bigglezink
  accept 5251                         -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  accept 5214                         -- Smokey LaRue
  accept 5243                         -- Leonid Barthalomew the Revered

step Terrordale: Egan
  when done strat-start
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Ride west across the zone to Terrordale: Egan waits in the westernmost of its three houses, where Group 28 found him. His blaster frees the ghosts of Stratholme.
  accept 5282                         -- Egan

step Stratholme: along the way
  when done strat-start
  along until strat-end
  tip Collected all through the city: Plagued Flesh Samples on the ghouls, the abominations and the crypt beasts (not on the skeletons); Stratholme Holy Water in the supply crates by the streets (some are trapped: plagued insects swarm out). Restless Souls: do not kill the Ghostly and Spectral Citizens; target one and use the blaster Egan gave you on it, then again on the soul that breaks free.
  note Share The Flesh Does Not Lie, The Archivist, The Great Ezra Grimm and Houses of the Holy with your group: click each in the quest log, then Share. The Restless Souls and Of Love and Family cannot be shared.
  collect 13174 quest 5212            -- Plagued Flesh Sample
  collect 13180 quest 5243            -- Stratholme Holy Water: supply crates
  kill 11122 quest 5282               -- Restless Soul, freed with the blaster

step Stratholme, first visit: before going in
  when done strat-start
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip First visit, the living side, by the main gate across the bridge: King's Square, Market Row, Crusaders' Square and the Scarlet Bastion, then Festival Lane and Elders' Square. Leave Balnazzar alive this time: The Archivist must be handed in before he dies, or his head starts nothing. Warcraft Tavern (written from Classic) says the doors of the Scarlet Bastion open with The Scarlet Key, from Arcanist Doan's chest in the Scarlet Monastery Library: to check in game.
  note In the quest log: The Flesh Does Not Lie (Betina), The Archivist (Duke Nicholas), The Great Ezra Grimm (Smokey LaRue), Houses of the Holy (Leonid), The Restless Souls (Egan); if taken in Group 30, Of Love and Family (Renfray). Not on this route: Sweet Serenity and Corruption (Winterspring), the dungeon set quests (Deliana, Anthion Harmon), Ras Frostwhisper's chain (Menethil's Gift).
  goto 26.5,10.4 map 1423 "Stratholme" r 25

step King's Square: Ezra Grimm
  when done strat-start
  tip Past the main gate, King's Square: follow the road round to the left to its dead end, under the sign of Ezra Grimm's Premium Tobacco. Ezra Grimm, undead (elite 61), stands in front of his shop.
  collect 13172 quest 5214            -- Grimm's Premium Tobacco: Ezra Grimm

step Market Row and Crusaders' Square
  when done strat-start
  tip Back through King's Square, then Market Row (Hearthsinger Forresten, rare, may walk there) to Crusaders' Square: Timmy the Cruel runs out once the square is cleared. Never click a pattern on the ground during a fight: it calls the Crimson Hammersmith. The Scarlet Bastion opens on the square.
  kill 10808 optional                 -- Timmy the Cruel

step The Scarlet Bastion: Malor's Strongbox
  when done strat-start
  tip In the Bastion, Malor the Zealous (elite 60) guards the Hoard: his strongbox, on the ground beside him, holds the Medallion of Faith. One medallion per run: whoever loots it keeps it for Aurius, in the third visit. Cannon Master Willey (elite 60) holds the armoury and calls riflemen: the cannons of his room fire on them.
  kill 11032 optional                 -- Malor the Zealous
  collect 12845 optional              -- Medallion of Faith: Malor's Strongbox

step The Scarlet Bastion: Archivist Galford
  when done strat-start
  tip Archivist Galford (elite 60) holds his library, across the hall from the last chamber, Balnazzar's: spread out against his fire. Once he is dead, use the Scarlet Archive, the book on the table behind him: the room burns. Leave Balnazzar for the second visit.
  kill 10811 quest 5251               -- Archivist Galford
  interact 176245 quest 5251          -- Scarlet Archive: set it on fire

step The Scarlet Bastion: the painting
  when done strat-start
  when onquest 5848
  tip Of Love and Family: an Unfinished Painting hangs on the wall of Galford's library, the twin moons on it; Renfray's painting is hidden behind it.
  collect 14679 quest 5848            -- Of Love and Family: behind the Unfinished Painting

step Festival Lane and Elders' Square
  label strat-v1-end
  when done strat-start
  tip Out of the Bastion, Festival Lane: The Unforgiven (elite 57) calls spirits, kill them first. Then Elders' Square: Magistrate Barthilas (elite 58) stands before Alonsus Chapel and drops the Key to the City. It opens the Service Entrance, the gate on this square, and the gate of the Gauntlet: one key in the group is enough. Leave the dungeon by the Service Entrance, or the way you came; keep the group together, without resetting the instance: the next two visits come back into it.
  kill 10435 optional                 -- Magistrate Barthilas
  collect 12382 optional              -- Key to the City: Magistrate Barthilas

step Light's Hope Chapel: Betina Bigglezink
  when complete 5212
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Ride back east to Light's Hope Chapel, a good ten minutes. Betina's next quest is for the third visit.
  turnin 5212                         -- Betina Bigglezink
  accept 5213                         -- The Scourge Data: a ziggurat of the dead side

step Light's Hope Chapel: Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  when complete 5251
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip The Archivist handed in: Balnazzar's head now starts the next quest (second visit).
  turnin 5251                         -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff

step Light's Hope Chapel: Smokey LaRue
  when complete 5214
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  turnin 5214                         -- Smokey LaRue

step Light's Hope Chapel: Leonid Barthalomew the Revered
  when complete 5243
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  turnin 5243                         -- Leonid Barthalomew the Revered

step Stratholme, second visit: Balnazzar
  when done strat-start
  tip Second visit: back into the same instance by the main gate, through the cleared streets to the Scarlet Bastion's last chamber. Grand Crusader Dathrohan (elite 62) turns into Balnazzar, a dread lord, during the fight: dispel his Deep Sleep, stand at range from his Psychic Scream. His head starts The Truth Comes Crashing Down for those who handed in The Archivist: right-click it.
  goto 26.5,10.4 map 1423 "Stratholme" r 25
  kill 10813 optional                 -- Balnazzar
  accept 5262                         -- Head of Balnazzar: Balnazzar

step Light's Hope Chapel: The Truth Comes Crashing Down
  label strat-v2-end
  when onquest 5262
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Out by the Service Entrance in Elders' Square (or the way you came) and back to Light's Hope Chapel. Duke Nicholas takes the head and sends you after Baron Rivendare, the last boss of the dead side: the third visit, in the same instance. Rather not ride again? Skip this step: Above and Beyond then waits for another run.
  turnin 5262                         -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  accept 5263

step Stratholme, third visit: before going in
  when done strat-start
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Third visit, the dead side: the Service Entrance, the gate east of the main one, opens with the Key to the City onto Elders' Square. Bosses 59 to 62: 60 advised. Opening the gate of the Gauntlet starts Baron Rivendare's 45-minute countdown: it only matters for Ysida Harmon (Dead Man's Plea, a dungeon set quest), no quest of this guide depends on it.
  note In the quest log: The Active Agent (Betina), Above and Beyond (Duke Nicholas). Whoever carries the Medallion of Faith: Aurius, just inside.
  enter "Stratholme" @26.5,10.4 map 1423

step Elders' Square: Aurius
  when done strat-start
  tip Aurius waits in Alonsus Chapel, on Elders' Square: the player with the Medallion of Faith hands it in, then takes Aurius' Reckoning. With the medallion handed in during this instance, Aurius joins the fight against Baron Rivendare. Whether he offers Aurius' Reckoning to the others of the group too: to check in game.
  accept 5122 optional                -- Aurius: with the Medallion of Faith
  turnin 5122 optional
  accept 5125 optional                -- Aurius

step The Gauntlet and the ziggurats
  when done strat-start
  tip The Key to the City opens the gate of the Gauntlet. Three ziggurats stand on the dead side, each with a guardian at its door: Nerub'enkan (the first, on the left), Baroness Anastari (the second: she possesses a player, bring them to half health), Maleki the Pallid (the third). Kill each guardian, then every Thuzadin Acolyte inside: the Scourge Data for Betina lies in a small box in one of the three. Stonespine (rare) may walk between the first two.
  kill 10437 optional                 -- Nerub'enkan
  kill 10436 optional                 -- Baroness Anastari
  kill 10438 optional                 -- Maleki the Pallid
  collect 13176 quest 5213            -- Scourge Data: a small box in one of the ziggurats

step Slaughter Square: Ramstein the Gorger
  when done strat-start
  tip With the three ziggurats cleared, the gates of Slaughter Square open. Kill every Bile Spewer and Venom Belcher in the square: Ramstein the Gorger (elite 61) comes out; he hits hard and knocks his target away. Then a horde of Mindless Undead, then three Black Guard Sentries at the door of the Slaughterhouse.
  kill 10439 optional                 -- Ramstein the Gorger

step The Slaughterhouse: Baron Rivendare
  label strat-v3-end
  when done strat-start
  tip Baron Rivendare (elite 62) raises skeletons and his Unholy Aura hurts everyone near him; his Mortal Strike cuts the tank's healing. His head is for Duke Nicholas. Then speak with Aurius for Aurius' Reckoning. The glowing symbol in front of the Baron, Menethil's Gift, belongs to Ras Frostwhisper's chain: not in this guide.
  collect 13251 quest 5263            -- Head of Baron Rivendare
  turnin 5125 optional                -- Aurius, after the fight

step Light's Hope Chapel: Betina Bigglezink
  when complete 5213
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Out of Stratholme, back east to Light's Hope Chapel.
  turnin 5213                         -- Betina Bigglezink

step Light's Hope Chapel: Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  when complete 5263
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Above and Beyond: Duke Nicholas sends you to Lord Maxwell Tyrosus, inside the chapel, who opens the Argent Hold, the chest beside him, for your reward.
  turnin 5263                         -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  accept 5264
  turnin 5264                         -- Lord Maxwell Tyrosus
  accept 5265
  turnin 5265                         -- The Argent Hold

step Light's Hope Chapel: what is left to hand in
  when onquest 5212,5214,5243,5251,5262
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Finished in the second or third visit only, or Balnazzar's head kept without the ride: hand them in now.
  turnin 5212 optional                -- Betina Bigglezink
  turnin 5214 optional                -- Smokey LaRue
  turnin 5243 optional                -- Leonid Barthalomew the Revered
  turnin 5251 optional                -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff
  turnin 5262 optional                -- Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff: the head of Balnazzar

step Terrordale: Egan
  when complete 5282
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip Ride west across the zone to Egan's house in Terrordale.
  turnin 5282                         -- Egan

step Tirion Fordring: Of Love and Family
  when complete 5848
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip West of Terrordale, Tirion's hut on the bank of the border river. His next quest, Find Myranda, leads to Hearthglen: not in this guide.
  turnin 5848                         -- Tirion Fordring

step Stratholme: quests not done
  label strat-end
  when done strat-start
  tip What is left of Stratholme in the quest log is for another run: keep it for one, or drop it to free the log.
  abandon 5212 optional
  abandon 5213 optional
  abandon 5214 optional
  abandon 5243 optional
  abandon 5251 optional
  abandon 5262 optional
  abandon 5263 optional
  abandon 5282 optional
  abandon 5125 optional
  abandon 5848 optional

# Groupe Alliance 0.12.0: Of Love and Family (5848), taken in Group 30 with its own question, when
# Stratholme was skipped: nothing brings the guide back to Tirion.
step Of Love and Family: not done
  when onquest 5848
  when !complete 5848
  tip Of Love and Family is not done and the guide does not go back to Stratholme: abandon it, or keep it for a run of your own.
  abandon 5848
